So... you're trapped beneath a level with Vecna and a Star Vampire on.

I have to say, if you're having trouble with nasties like this then
you're probably a little deep for your current strength. You need
better AC and more spank-power. Extra HP is always a good thing as
well.

To do this without wishing or polying (does "upgrading" armour using
!oGL count as polying?) is not going to be easy, and will probably
involve you dragging yourself deeper into the dungeons in search of
decent kit. Is there any potentially interesting un-IDed gear in any
shops you have already passed? Also make sure to dig up all graves and
search for doorless cupboards and cash vaults.

In your case though, having both command undead and create monster,
I'd think about going to the (now empty) Vecna's lair and having a
create/kill spree there. I believe much of what is created will be
undead, so you will have a constant supply of pets to help you kill
the rest. The monsters created will be fairly high level as well, so
there's a good chance of getting worthwhile armour, potions,
spellbooks & scrolls off them.

If you can't raise your AC to avoid those big hits from V&V, consider
invisibility or (better) displacement. That will help. controlled
teleport (or at least teleport-at-will) will make a big difference as
well. As long as you have charges/pow you can always stay a step ahead
of them, or at least make it to the upstairs without them following.
The vampire at least should respect the big E. Don't know about Vecna.

If you can make it to Grund's, you can make good use of the landmines
and grenades that can be found in abundance there. Set up a load of
traps and then lure Vecna/vampy onto them. Again, controlled teleport
would be very useful here (create a "circle" of mines and the 'port
into the middle of it then wait for them to arrive.) That's how I tend
to deal with my quest nemeses these days. Getting your hands on
hellfire helps as well- My current wizard blasted the Dark One to
ashes with that baby =-)

Not sure what other advice to offer, really. The thing with Slashem is
to take it slow: move forward, collect gear until almost-burdened,
then bring it all back to your stash and/or altar to sort through, ID
and apply where necessary. Rinse, repeat, die choking on a can of
spinach just as you're ready to begin your ascension run (yeah, I've
actually done that.)

